                                 PRESENTS

                             FateComment V2.1
                 A Comment Tool for CNet V2.63 and higher
                          (C) 1994 by Fate/Logic
                         Release Date: 23.06.1994


COPYRIGHT
=========

     This Tool is Copyright (C)1994 by Fate/Logic. Freely usable.
     Nobody is allowed to modify the Tool or this Docfile.


WHAT'S IT?
==========

     Guess... it's a Replacement for the "F" Command, which allows you
     to leave Comments to one of the Sysops or Subops. The Advantage
     to the "MS" Command is that you don't have to remember their Names
     and you don't need to specify a Subject.

     Probably the biggest Advantage is that it makes it easier for
     new Users to send Mail to the Sysop Team.


FEATURES
========

     + Multi-Comment allows you to leave Comments to the whole Team.
     + 100% safe against Errors (see "ERROR-SAFETY").
     + Easy to use, especially for new Users.
     + Nice Design.


INSTALLATION
============

     Because of a Change between CNet v2.63 and v3.05c concerning the
     CALLEDITOR Command I had to include two Versions. If you're still
     using v2.63 'FateComment263' is the right one, else try using
     'FateComment305'. Rename the File to 'FateComment'.

     Move 'FateComment' and 'FateComment.cfg' into your 'PFiles:'
     Directory. Next load your favourite Text Editor and perform the
     following Changes in Section 2 ("Avaible everywhere"):

     1. Change 'Feedback' into '!Feedback'
     2. Go to the End of the Section and add:
        <TAB>Feedback |<CTRL-Q>#0PFiles:Feedback}
     
     Press TAB at the START of the Line, no leading Spaces!

     Now load the File 'FateComment.cfg' into the Editor.
     Every User requires three Lines.

     Line 1: Account Number
     Line 2: Handle
     Line 3: A Comment

     Here's an Example Configfile:

-----cut here------------------------------------------------------------
     1
     Fate
     How can I help you?
     4
     Example User
     Example Comment
     19
     Gizmo
     Amiga Subboard Operator
-----cut here------------------------------------------------------------


ERROR-SAFETY
============

     The Comment a User enters is sent as normal Mail. If the Receiver's
     Mailbox is closed, the Account has been killed or the Configfile is
     corrupt, your Comment is NOT lost. FateComment will attempt to save
     it in your own Mailbox, so you don't have to write it again!


HISTORY
=======

     V1.0      11.2.94   First Release

     V2.0      14.6.94   Total Rewrite
                         Added Multi-Comment and removed the max. Editor
                         Lines Limit which now depends on the User.

     V2.1      23.6.94   Bugfix
                         Aborting the Editor would be ignored under v2.63
                         due to a Change to the CALLEDITOR Command. Fixed.


